### API-35 Test Assertion Hardening & Full Regression Verification (Commit `7ea8774`)

As requested in the peer review, test assertions in `server/tests/lab-03/users-admin.api.test.ts` for test **API-35** have been strengthened to rigorously verify both possible event sequence outcomes:

```ts
// 1. Assert assignRes never returns 500 or unexpected codes
expect([200, 400]).toContain(assignRes.status);

// 2. Assert ticketOwnerId is strictly null in database
expect(finalTicket?.ticketOwnerId).toBeNull();

if (assignRes.status === 200) {
  // Case A: Assignment succeeded first (200), then deactivation cascaded and unassigned it
  expect(deactivateRes.body.unassignedTicketsCount).toBe(1);
  // Version incremented by assignment (1 -> 2) and by cascade unassignment (2 -> 3)
  expect(finalTicket?.version).toBe(3);
} else {
  // Case B: Deactivation succeeded first (unassigned count 0), assignment rejected (400)
  expect(assignRes.status).toBe(400);
  expect(assignRes.body.error).toBe("Validation failed");
  expect(assignRes.body.details?.ownerId).toBe("Owner must be an active IT Staff or Administrator");
  expect(deactivateRes.body.unassignedTicketsCount).toBe(0);
  // Version remains at initial version (1)
  expect(finalTicket?.version).toBe(1);
}
```

### Full Live Regression Verification Results
All suites executed against isolated disposable database `toktickit_test`:
- **Server Test Suite:** 25 files, 254/254 tests passed (100%).
- **Client Test Suite:** 15 files, 80/80 tests passed (100%).
- **Playwright E2E Suite:** 69/69 tests passed across Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile viewports (100%).
- **TypeScript Builds:** Server and client builds passed with 0 errors.

All Phase F4 work packages (P11 & P12) are fully proven and ready for reviewer approval and merge into `lab3-staging`.
